er reason has his helmet off  for the entire Feast despite all the  other kingsguard having their helmets on  in the background now this is actually a  very important factor for what happens  later so I don't know why sir Christian  has his off despite him saying he's on  on duty not only this but sir Christian  is just staring at Rainier with an upset  expression for a very long duration so  any dimwit with eyes could piece  together what he's feeling to me it just  comes across as the writers needing a  way for Joffrey to naturally figure out  that sir Christian is obsessed with  renera so they can have a contrived  confrontation and then after this I  guess sir Christian just breaks out of  nowhere and beats the life out of  Joffrey why didn't anyone stop him why  are the guards in the background just  standing there why is this entire  wedding turning into a violent mosh but  after sir Christian attacks one person  what is happening right now there's so  many aspects about this whole scenario  that just doesn't make sense to me now  the issue isn't the presentation that is  supposed to be intentionally confusing  due to the perspective we're witnessing  the event from but more of the logic  behind everything and the character  motivations also is he still technically  a King's Guard after this whole scenario  shouldn't they be putting him in holding  there's so much confusion around all of  this and I desperately need them to  address this in the next episode  although I kind of doubt that's going to  happen since they seem to be doing a  major time Jump I've seen some counter  arguments that the kingsguard have high  Authority and no one questions their  judgment so sir Kirsten doing this is  passable because he can say that Joffrey  pulled a knife on rhaenyra which firstly  sir Christian is already upset that he's  damaging his honor so lying on top of  everything would theoretically make  things worse and secondly there are  dozens of witnesses close by that 