 to only run into her  and no one else or was he scouting in  the mountains or something and quickly  came down I don't know I'm thinking  about this more critically since sir  Christian kind of set me off but the  scene ends with a banger match cut so  any small flaw Is Forgiven  Otto Hightower has one quick dialogue  scene with Allison and is easily one of  my favorite scenes in the episode it's  emotionally charged throughout Otto is  further manipulating Allison by stoking  her fears and the information that  Ranier will possibly kill Allison's  children is heartbreaking I really hope  this isn't the last we see of Otto  because I adore the man a different  mirror succeeds in war will follow do  you understand hopefully when visceros  eventually passes away which is taking a  really long time since the man is  showing up in the next episode even with  the big time Jump Then Otto Hightower  can finally come back to King's Landing  going into the targaryens meeting up  with the valerions it feels ironic that  I like these setup scenes just as much  as the wedding payoff because there are  a lot of good moments here like the  subtle detail of laner's sword fighting  with his lover eluding early on that  he's gay the breathtaking coats that  Ranier and later are walking down and  both of the dialogue scenes within the  kingdom seeing cordless awkwardly step  around the succession conflict without  trying to be rude was very cute and the  tug of war between them trying to come  to an equal Arrangement was well written  the scene after this keeps the quality  going or rainy's makes a smart  observation that they are putting their  family in danger by teaming up with  renera it's kind of weird how ignorant  Corliss is towards that and even his  son's homophobia I'd assume he'd be a  bit smarter but I guess the man is  pretty obsessed with gaining more power  since he came from nothing in his blind  decided by those things then for the  last standout scene we have viserys's  monologue where he talks about his  regrets and his overall lasting image  it's heartbreaking to see this man on  his final leg suffering a painful death  but he's enduring all of this anguish so  he can try to be a better ruler and be  remembered despite all of his flaws and  making mistakes that's one aspect of his  character that's extremely commendable  he's so wholesome that he wants everyone  to love him and seeing him thinking  about different ways his life could have  played out is intriguing the  cinematography where the camera slowly  pushes in on visceros is a great touch  and really makes us empathize more with  him even Lionel strong during the scene  offers a good perspective where he says  it's better to have a peaceful role  instead of having a war and being  remembered for it that man is turning  out to be a great hand so far and seems  to be one of the only people not acting  selfishly at least so far it also makes  me wonder in the scene if the mazers are  intentionally failing at curing faceres  and and that tying into the whole  maester conspiracy of them disliking the  targaryens and overall having the power  to drastically affect people in power  because even if that's not the case you  can still kind of read into that going  back to the wedding dinner even though I  disliked the Christian Cole aspect of  the wedding there are still some other  great aspects that don't make the scene  really bad Damon and Allison being  showstoppers really spices up the  wedding and adds some conflict into the  mix especially Allison literally just  coming in to make a statement that she's  pissed off and means business and Damon  showing up increases the quality of any  scene in the show the moment between  Damon and Sir Gerald Royce Was Juicy in  which Damon essentially Uno reverse  cards sergelled wanting to have him  executed by countering with inheriting  all of Lady raya's Land Sergio's  reaction to that was golden and further  cements Damon as a cunning player in the  series then the overall attention to  detail was astounding with the set  decorations the amount of characters on  display and all of the interactions  between them shooting this scene must  have been a very daunting task I think  the execution of it ended up being  pretty good besides the circustin  portion of it obviously and before  ending the video it feels crazy to me  that we're already transitioning to the  older actors like it's only been five  episodes so far and we've gone through  years of their lives this feeling may be  more noticeable if we were watching  these episodes all at once but since  we're waiting a week between each  episode the time jumps may not feel as  noticeable but so far the pace feels a  bit jarring at times especially in the  case of Sir Christian Cole's  relationship with rainera because we go  from them having sex for the first time  two sir Kristen immediately shooting his  shot as if they've been lovers for a  long time regardless though the casting  director is working overtime and finding  outstanding actors to keep replacing  these characters even Lena valerion was  just replaced for this episode and in  the next one she's being replaced again  but overall I think the writing  surrounding Kirsten Cole was pretty  contrived and stereotypical and I  previously hoped they wouldn't go down  this road besides that one shortcoming  the episode was still really good and  thank you for watching let me know what  you thought about episode 5 in the  comments

